================================================================================
LESSON 8: SHOWING BOOKS ON SCREEN IN REACT
================================================================================


LESSON OVERVIEW
================================================================================

This lesson explains how to display books fetched from an API on the screen.

Main concepts:

- Store books in React state
- Use map() to loop through books
- Extract information from volumeInfo
- Create one UI card for each book
- Display title, author, publisher, description, and image
- Handle missing API fields
- Use optional chaining
- Provide fallback values
- Use Bootstrap cards and responsive grids
- Handle loading, error, no-results, and success states


================================================================================
1. WHAT DOES "SHOWING BOOKS ON SCREEN" MEAN?
================================================================================

The API gives us book data as JavaScript objects.

Example:

{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "abc123",
      "volumeInfo": {
        "title": "JavaScript: The Good Parts",
        "authors": ["Douglas Crockford"],
        "publisher": "O'Reilly Media",
        "publishedDate": "2008-05-01",
        "description": "Book description...",
        "pageCount": 172,
        "categories": ["Computers"],
        "imageLinks": {
          "thumbnail": "book-image-url"
        },
        "previewLink": "google-books-preview-url"
      }
    }
  ]
}


Our job is to convert this data into UI elements.

Flow:

API Response
     |
     v
data.items
     |
     v
setBooks(bookList)
     |
     v
books State
     |
     v
books.map(...)
     |
     v
Create Book Cards
     |
     v
Display on Screen


