================================================================================

Bootstrap uses a 12-column grid.

Example:

<div className="row">

  <div className="col-md-4">
    Book
  </div>

</div>


col-md-4 means:

12 / 4 = 3


Therefore:

3 cards per row at the md breakpoint and above.


Common layouts:

-------------+------------------------+-----------------------------
Class        | Width                  | Typical Layout
-------------+------------------------+-----------------------------
col-12       | 12 / 12 = 100%        | 1 card per row
col-sm-6     |  6 / 12 = 50%         | 2 cards per row
col-md-4     |  4 / 12 = 33.33%      | 3 cards per row
col-lg-3     |  3 / 12 = 25%         | 4 cards per row
-------------+------------------------+-----------------------------


A good responsive combination:

className="col-12 col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-3 mb-4"


Meaning:

Mobile:
-> 1 book per row

Small:
-> 2 books per row

Medium:
-> 3 books per row

Large:
-> 4 books per row


