18. CONDITIONAL RENDERING STATES
================================================================================

The application should normally handle four UI states:

1. Loading
2. Error
3. No Results
4. Success


----------------+--------------------------------------+-----------------------
State           | Condition                            | UI
----------------+--------------------------------------+-----------------------
Loading         | isLoading                            | Loading books...
Error           | error                                | Error message
No Results      | !isLoading && !error && !books.length| No books found
Success         | !isLoading && !error && books.length | Book cards
----------------+--------------------------------------+-----------------------


================================================================================
19. LOADING STATE
================================================================================

{isLoading && (

  <div className="alert alert-info">
    Loading books...
  </div>

)}


Purpose:

- Tells the user that data is being fetched.
- Avoids displaying an apparently empty screen.


================================================================================
20. ERROR STATE
================================================================================

{error && (

  <div className="alert alert-danger">

    Error: {error}

  </div>

)}


Purpose:

- Displays API/network errors.
- Makes failures understandable to the user.


================================================================================
21. NO RESULTS STATE
================================================================================

{!isLoading &&
 !error &&
 books.length === 0 && (

  <div className="alert alert-warning">

    No books found.
    Try another search.

  </div>

)}


Purpose:

- Distinguishes "no results" from an application error.


================================================================================
22. SUCCESS STATE
================================================================================

{!isLoading &&
 !error &&
 books.length > 0 && (

  <div className="row">

    {books.map((book) => (

      // Book card

    ))}

  </div>

)}


Purpose:

- Displays cards only when valid book results are available.


================================================================================
23. COMPLETE BOOK DISPLAY CODE
================================================================================

function BookList({
  books,
  isLoading,
  error,
  searchTerm
}) {

  if (isLoading) {

    return (
      <div className="alert alert-info">
        Loading books...
      </div>
    );

  }


  if (error) {

    return (
      <div className="alert alert-danger">
        Error: {error}
      </div>
    );

  }


  if (books.length === 0) {

    return (
      <div className="alert alert-warning">

        No books found for "{searchTerm}".

      </div>
    );

  }


  return (

    <div>

      <p className="text-muted">

        Found <strong>{books.length}</strong> books

      </p>


      <div className="row">

        {books.map((book) => {

          const info = book.volumeInfo || {};

          return (

            <div
              key={book.id}
              className="
                col-12
                col-sm-6
                col-md-4
                col-lg-3
                mb-4
              "
            >

              <div className="card h-100 shadow-sm">


                {info.imageLinks?.thumbnail && (

                  <img
                    src={info.imageLinks.thumbnail}
                    className="card-img-top"
                    alt={info.title || 'Book cover'}
                    style={{
                      height: '250px',
                      objectFit: 'cover'
                    }}
                  />

                )}


                <div className="card-body d-flex flex-column">


                  <h5 className="card-title">

                    {info.title || 'No Title'}

                  </h5>


                  <p className="card-text text-muted">

                    <strong>Author:</strong>{' '}

                    {info.authors?.join(', ')
                      || 'Unknown Author'}

                  </p>


                  {info.publisher && (

                    <p className="card-text small">

                      <strong>Publisher:</strong>{' '}
                      {info.publisher}

                    </p>

                  )}


                  {info.publishedDate && (

                    <p className="card-text small">

                      <strong>Published:</strong>{' '}
                      {info.publishedDate}

                    </p>

                  )}


                  {info.pageCount && (

                    <p className="card-text small">

                      <strong>Pages:</strong>{' '}
                      {info.pageCount}

                    </p>

                  )}


                  {info.categories?.length > 0 && (

                    <p className="card-text small">

                      <strong>Category:</strong>{' '}

                      {info.categories.join(', ')}

                    </p>

                  )}


                  <p className="card-text small flex-grow-1">

                    {info.description
                      ? `${info.description.substring(0, 150)}...`
                      : 'No description available'}

                  </p>


                  {info.previewLink && (

                    <a
                      href={info.previewLink}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      className="btn btn-primary btn-sm mt-auto"
                    >

                      View on Google Books

                    </a>

                  )}

                </div>

              </div>

            </div>

          );

        })}

      </div>

    </div>

  );

}

export default BookList;


